  "description": "Marinated chicken thighs, properly stir-fried peppers and celery, roasted peanuts, and a sweet, sour, and savory sauce make for the best restaurant-style kung pao chicken recipe.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: vegetable oil → peanut oil or canola oil; dried red Chinese chiles → Arbol chiles\n\nNotes: If you can't find boneless skinless chicken thighs, you can debone them yourself using this guide. Shaoxing wine can be found in most Asian markets. If unavailable, dry sherry can be used in its place. If you can't find whole dried chiles, substitute with 1/4 teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes.",
